-- title:
--   Node stalk over a second DVR: injectivity, coordinates, evaluation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a divisibility $p \mid M$; assume $p^2 \nmid M$ (`hpM2`), that $H$ contains every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$ (`hHp`), and that $M/p \neq 0$. Let `hj` record that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral weight-zero ratios at full level, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over the coefficient ring `R p`; among its data are a curve model `𝔛.Meta` of the geometric function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, an integral proper smooth relative-dimension-one curve `(𝔛.Meta).C` over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with a ring isomorphism `(𝔛.Meta).ffEquiv` from `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` onto its function field and a bijection of its closed points with the places of the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an isomorphism `𝔛.eeta` from `(𝔛.Meta).C` to the base change of the model along `R p → AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   Valuation data: $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, whose residue field is assumed algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : \mathrm{R}\,p \to A$ is a ring homomorphism lifting the structure map $\mathrm{R}\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ along $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`).
--
--   First coefficient ring: $O$ is a discrete valuation ring (a domain), $\rho_O : \mathrm{R}\,p \to O$, the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$ (`hϖ`), $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$ satisfies $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$ (`htoκ`), $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $j_O \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map (`hjO`), and $\iota_A : O \to A$ satisfies $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\iota_A$ equals $j_O$ (`hιA`) and $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \iota_A = \mathrm{to}\kappa$ (`hιAκ`).
--
--   The node: $n$ is a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` supplied by the package, whose common target is the fibre of the model over $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$; writing `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ` for the base-change morphism from that fibre to $X_O :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the point
--   $$x_n := (\text{pullback.fst} \ggg \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0 \ggg \mathrm{bcMap})(n)$$
--   of $X_O$ is the crossing point under consideration (here $\ggg$ denotes composition in diagrammatic order).
--
--   Crossing chart: $e \ge 1$, $U$ is an open subscheme of $X_O$ containing $x_n$ (`hxU`), and $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)\bigr)$, the crossing scheme `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme (((p : ℕ) : O) ^ e)`, is a morphism over $O$ in the sense that $f$ followed by the structure morphism of the crossing scheme equals $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ followed by the projection $X_O \to \operatorname{Spec}O$ (`hover`). The further hypotheses on $f$ are: `hfib`, that for a point $y$ of $U$ the two coordinates `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` both lie in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $y$ maps to $x_n$; `hpt`, that at every $y$ of $U$ lying over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism on residue fields; `het`, that every such $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V$ in $U$ with $V \hookrightarrow U$ followed by $f$ étale; and `hor₁`–`hor₄`, that for $y$ in $U$ the coordinate `CrossingQuotient.V` lies in $f(y)$ if and only if the image of $y$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0 ≫ bcMap …`, and `CrossingQuotient.U` lies in $f(y)$ if and only if that image lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1 ≫ bcMap …`.
--
--   Second coefficient ring: $O'$ is a discrete valuation ring (a domain), $\sigma : O \to O'$, $\iota_{A'} : O' \to A$ with $\iota_{A'} \circ \sigma = \iota_A$ (`hσ`), $\iota_{A'}$ injective (`hιA'inj`) and local (`hιA'loc`), $j_{O'} : O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $j_{O'} \circ (\sigma \circ \rho_O)$ the structure map of $\mathrm{R}\,p$ (`hjO'`), $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\iota_{A'}$ equal to $j_{O'}$ (`hιA'j`), and $(\mathrm{res}_A \circ \iota_{A'}) \circ (\sigma \circ \rho_O) = \mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$ (`htoκ'`).
--
--   Abbreviations introduced in the statement: $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ is the base change of the model along $\mathrm{R}\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $\mathrm{prJ} : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_O$ is induced by $j_O$; `VM` is the open $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}^{-1}(\mathrm{prJ}^{-1}(U))$ of `(𝔛.Meta).C`; $Q = O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ with $\varphi$ the identification of $Q$ with the global sections of its spectrum; $g_v$ and $g_u$ are the sections of $X_O$ over the open image $U.\iota({\top})$ obtained by pulling back the coordinates `CrossingQuotient.V` and `CrossingQuotient.U` along $f$ and transporting along the isomorphism $\Gamma(U,\top) \cong \Gamma(X_O, U.\iota(\top))$; $\mathrm{bc}'$ is the base-change morphism from the fibre over $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$ to $X_{O'} :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)`; $x_n'$ is the image of $n$ under `pullback.fst ≫ 𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0 ≫ bc'`, the crossing point read over $O'$; $\mathrm{prJ}' : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_{O'}$ is induced by $j_{O'}$ and $\mathrm{pr}_\sigma : X_{O'} \to X_O$ by $\sigma$; $B$ is the stalk of $X_{O'}$ at $x_n'$; and $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ is the structure map, namely $O' \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}O',\top)$ followed by pullback along $X_{O'} \to \operatorname{Spec}O'$ and then the germ at $x_n'$.
--
--   The assertion is made for every proof `hgen` that the generic point of `(𝔛.Meta).C` lies in $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}^{-1}(\mathrm{prJ}^{-1}(U.\iota(\top)))$, with the reading homomorphism
--   $$\mathrm{read} : \Gamma(X_O, U.\iota(\top)) \to \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H$$
--   defined as pullback along $\mathrm{prJ}$, then along $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, then the germ at the generic point (landing in the function field of `(𝔛.Meta).C`), followed by `(𝔛.Meta).ffEquiv.symm`; one puts $\mathrm{param} := \mathrm{read}(g_v)$ and $\mathrm{param}' := \mathrm{read}(g_u)$. It is made further for every proof `hsp` that the image of the generic point under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and then $\mathrm{prJ}'$ specialises to $x_n'$, with
--   $$\mathrm{emb} : B \to \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H$$
--   defined as the specialisation map of stalks along `hsp`, then the stalk map of $\mathrm{prJ}'$, then the stalk map of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, followed by `(𝔛.Meta).ffEquiv.symm`.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of three clauses.
--
--   First: $\sigma_B$ is a local homomorphism, $\mathrm{emb}$ is injective, and $\mathrm{emb} \circ \sigma_B$ equals the structure map $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` composed with $j_{O'}$.
--
--   Second: $x_n'$ lies in $\mathrm{pr}_\sigma^{-1}(U.\iota(\top))$, and for that membership the germ at $x_n'$ of the pullback of $g_v$ along $\mathrm{pr}_\sigma$ has $\mathrm{emb}$-image $\mathrm{param}$, while the germ at $x_n'$ of the pullback of $g_u$ has $\mathrm{emb}$-image $\mathrm{param}'$.
--
--   Third: for every place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, a valuation subring of the function field containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring — which is rational, in the sense that $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ maps onto the residue field of $W$, and for every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec}A \to U$ such that $s$ followed by $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ and the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}O$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_A$, such that $\operatorname{Spec}(A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ followed by $s$ and $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ coincides with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of `(𝔛.Meta).C` corresponding to $W$ under `(𝔛.Meta).pointEquivPlace` followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{prJ}$, and such that $s$ sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A$ to $x_n$: then for every morphism $s' : \operatorname{Spec}A \to X_{O'}$ agreeing with $s$ on the first projection (that is, $s'$ followed by $X_{O'} \to X$ equals $s$ followed by $U \hookrightarrow X_O \to X$) and with $s'$ followed by $X_{O'} \to \operatorname{Spec}O'$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_{A'}$, the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A$ is sent by $s'$ to $x_n'$, and, $\chi : B \to A$ being the composite of the specialisation map of stalks for this equality with `Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo s'`, the homomorphism $\chi$ is local, $\chi \circ \sigma_B = \iota_{A'}$, and for every $b \in B$ the element $\mathrm{emb}(b)$ lies in the valuation subring of $W$ and $W.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{emb}(b))$ — the element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose image in the residue field of $W$ is the residue of $\mathrm{emb}(b)$ — equals the image of $\chi(b)$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the transport step in the analysis of a node of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$: it compares the local ring of the crossing point after base change to a second discrete valuation ring $O'$ with the geometric function field, identifies the two crossing coordinates of the étale chart inside that field, and identifies the value at a rational place with the specialisation of the corresponding section of $\operatorname{Spec}A$. It is used in the proofs of [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isUnit_and_read_eq_and_ord_placeOn_eq_zero_of_forall_ord_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit_evalAt_of_chart_of_residue_surjective) and of [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_and_forall_section_exists_ringHom_evalAt_eq_of_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_and_forall_section_exists_ringHom_evalAt_eq_of_chart), and it cites the integrality of `XO` over such a coefficient ring, the surjectivity of the residue field map of the crossing scheme at its singular point, and a uniqueness criterion for points of a fibre product.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_injective_stalkRead_and_stalkRead_germ_eq_read_chart_and_forall_section_evalAt_stalkRead_eq_of_chart.lean

